output:
@Deirdre Fortuin thank you for asking rather than just announcing it — I really appreciate that. I'm not going to fight the allocation. I get that it's a numbers thing and that Bronwyn needs the help more with 24 little ones. But I'm gutted, honestly, and I don't want to pretend I'm fine about it. Noma's been in the Seahorses with me for three years, since my first year teaching, and she basically trained me — sign-in sheets, the parent WhatsApp group, all of it without me losing my mind. She does the isiXhosa songs at morning ring and the kids ask for "Noma's song" every day. When Zayd had his meltdowns in Term 2, she was the only one who could calm him; she sat with him under the jungle gym. So this one really matters to me and to the room.

If you're able to put two practical things to SMT, I'd be grateful. First, could Charlene come in for a day or two in the last week of term (1–4 Dec) to meet Noma and see the routine before she starts on 11 Jan? Schools open on 14 Jan, and the first weeks of Grade R are the hardest — new kids crying at the gate, and a new assistant plus a new group all at once is a lot. Second, could Noma pop in for morning ring in the first week back, from 14 Jan, even just for 15 minutes? She'll still be just across the courtyard in Grade 00, and Luthando and Mia in next year's group already know her from aftercare.

I know nothing is final until Friday, so thank you for making space for this and for not just announcing it.
